---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "When should a business consider custom software?",
    answer:
      "Custom software becomes worth considering when existing products cannot support important workflows without excessive manual work, duplicate systems or compromises that materially affect the business.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals replace spreadsheet-based processes?",
    answer:
      "Yes, where the process is suitable. We first understand what the spreadsheets are doing, who uses them and which rules need to become part of a structured application.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can new software integrate with our existing systems?",
    answer:
      "Usually, where suitable APIs, databases or other integration methods are available. Integration requirements should be included in the architecture from the beginning.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can software be developed in phases?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Larger systems often benefit from phased delivery so the most important workflows can be validated before additional modules are introduced.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Who owns the custom software?",
    answer:
      "Ownership and licensing terms should be defined in the project agreement. For bespoke projects, those terms can be structured according to the agreed commercial arrangement.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Does custom software need ongoing maintenance?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Dependencies, infrastructure, integrations, security requirements and business workflows change over time, so production software requires ongoing technical attention.",
  },
];
---

<section class="software-faq">
  <div class="site-container software-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Software development FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before replacing the workaround with a system.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="software-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .software-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .software-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(16rem, 0.68fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .software-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .software-faq h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .software-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .software-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .software-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .software-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .software-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
